From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msado15: Recordset.Filter is a view of the rows (criteria, bookmarks, FilterGroupEnum).

A criteria string hid every row ("No filter performed. Reporting no records found."). As ADO's client cursor does, the rows a filter does not show are set aside with their places and come back where they were when the filter changes or goes. Criteria are clauses "field op value" (=, <>, <, >, <=, >=, LIKE) joined by AND and OR and grouped with parentheses; text compares without case; values are 'text', numbers (a $ allowed), #dates# (month/day/year) and NULL, and IS [NOT] NULL; Null matches no other comparison. An array of bookmarks and adFilterPendingRecords, adFilterFetchedRecords, adFilterConflictingRecords (none: a batch stops at its first failure) are filters too. The filter's first row becomes the current one; RecordCount, AbsolutePosition and the moves are the filter's rows; a bookmark is a row's place without the filter, so bookmarks stay valid as filters come and go (put_Bookmark, Move, Find, GetRows). A change, Delete and AddNew under a filter are kept in their rows; Sort sorts every row with the filter's view after it; UpdateBatch and CancelBatch with adAffectAll take the hidden rows too, adAffectGroup only the shown ones; Delete adAffectGroup deletes the shown rows; Requery and Resync keep the filter. Bookmarks a script passes by reference are taken. The msado15 test's unknown-field filter now fails with adErrItemNotFound, as on Windows (todo_wine removed).
